# The Sifting Box's tub faces, and the water that turns it into an Ice-o-lator.
#
# PLACEHOLDER art. Warlon Mhite may redraw these; that is what the .mctex is for.
#
# A coopered tub: vertical staves and two iron hoops. That silhouette is load-bearing rather than
# decorative -- this block holds a bucket of water when it is running as an Ice-o-lator, and a
# slatted crate visibly would not. Barrels are how Minecraft already draws "a wooden thing that
# holds liquid", so the block says what it can do before a tooltip does.
#
# The palette is hemp planks and hemp canvas, sampled from the mod's own textures, so it sits next
# to the rest of the wood set. The screen face (block/sifting_box_screen) and the kief
# (block/sifting_box_kief) are drawn in sifting_box.mctex -- they are the same mesh and the same
# powder whichever mode is running.
#
# Block faces are low contrast on purpose (vanilla blocks span a median 76 luminance steps against
# an item's 164).

@palette wood
. = none
1 = 3F3A26      stave seam, darker than any plank tone so the staves read
2 = 5A5236
3 = 67603E
4 = 82794E
5 = 8A8155
6 = 948A5E
7 = A1976C
i = 41403C      iron hoop, shadowed lower edge
j = 5E5D57      iron hoop body
k = 7C7A72      iron hoop highlight

# The tub wall: vertical staves, banded by two hoops. The seams sit every four pixels so the
# staves tile without a visible repeat at the block edge.
@texture block/sifting_box_side 16x16 type=block tiling=true
1654165516441655
1546166414561664
kjkkjkjkkjkkjkjk
ijiijijiijiijiji
1655164516541645
1546165616641556
1664154616551464
1455166516441665
1656144616541656
1544165616651454
kjkkjkjkkjkkjkjk
ijiijijiijiijiji
1655165416451655
1464155616641546
1556166414551664
1645154616551456

# The rim you see from above: the tops of the staves, with the upper hoop's iron showing at the
# outer edge. The mesh is drawn by the separate inside face, not by this one.
@texture block/sifting_box_top 16x16 type=block tiling=true
kjkkjkjkkjkkjkjk
j655164516541645
k546165616641556
j664154616551464
k455166516441665
j656144616541656
k544165616651454
j655165416451655
k464155616641546
j556166414551664
k645154616551456
j654165516441655
k546166414561664
j664156416551464
k455165516441665
kjkkjkjkkjkkjkjk

# The water surface, drawn as one flat quad inside the tub when FILLED is true. Slush rather than
# clear water: this tub is packed in ice by definition, so there are floating shards in it, and
# they are what make the surface read as *cold* rather than as a swimming pool.
#
# The palette is sampled up from vanilla's own ice tones towards white for the shards. Deliberately
# a narrow band -- water read at block contrast is nearly flat, and a high-contrast surface would
# fight the frost particles the block already emits.
@palette water
w = 3E5F86      the deep between shards
x = 4E739B      body
y = 6E97BE      lit ripple
z = A9CBE0      a floating shard, catching the light
@texture block/sifting_box_water 16x16 type=block tiling=true palette=water
xxwxxzzxxxwwxxxx
